    "id": "train-6550",
    "question": "In a car dealership with 600 cars, 60% of the cars are hybrids, and 40% of the hybrids contain only one headlight. How many of the hybrids have full headlights?",
    "gold": "216",
    "answer": "In the car dealership with 600 cars, 60% of the cars are hybrids, meaning there are 60/100*600 = <<60/100*600=360>>360 hybrid cars.\nOut of the 360 hybrid cars, 40% contain only one headlight. a total of 40/100*360 = <<40/100*360=144>>144 cars.\nThe total number of hybrid cars with full headlights is 360-144=<<360-144=216>>216\n#### 216"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many of the hybrids have full headlights, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of hybrids in the dealership.\n2. Determine the number of hybrids that contain only one headlight.\n3. Subtract the number of hybrids that contain only one headlight from the total number of hybrids to find the number of hybrids that have full headlights.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of hybrids.\nThe dealership has 600 cars in total, and 60% of them are hybrids.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of hybrids} = 60\\% \\times 600 = 0.60 \\times 600 = 360\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of hybrids that contain only one headlight.\n40% of the hybrids contain only one headlight.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of hybrids with only one headlight} = 40\\% \\times 360 = 0.40 \\times 360 = 144\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Subtract the number of hybrids that contain only one headlight from the total number of hybrids to find the number of hybrids that have full headlights.\n\\[\n\\text{Number of hybrids with full headlights} = 360 - 144 = 216\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of hybrids that have full headlights is \\boxed{216}.",
